import{_ as s,o as a,c as i,an as t}from"./chunks/framework.BeqddKcr.js";const u=JSON.parse('{"title":"Hardware Configuration","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"configuration/hardware.md","filePath":"configuration/hardware.md","lastUpdated":null}'),n={name:"configuration/hardware.md"};function o(l,e,r,h,p,d){return a(),i("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[t(`<h1 id="Hardware-Configuration" tabindex="-1">Hardware Configuration <a class="header-anchor" href="#Hardware-Configuration" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Hardware Configuration {#Hardware-Configuration}&quot;">​</a></h1><p>Legate manages the processors and memory used by cuNumeric.jl. By default it detects the available hardware and reserves most of its resources. On a shared machine, or when running several Julia processes, explicitly limit each process&#39;s allocation to avoid competing for the same CPUs, GPUs, and memory.</p><p>Set environment variables <strong>before starting Julia</strong>. The runtime reads its configuration once during initialization. Changing <code>ENV</code> after <code>using cuNumeric</code> does not reconfigure it. Restart Julia to apply changes. The shell examples below use Bash on Linux.</p><h2 id="Automatic-and-manual-configuration" tabindex="-1">Automatic and manual configuration <a class="header-anchor" href="#Automatic-and-manual-configuration" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Automatic and manual configuration {#Automatic-and-manual-configuration}&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th style="text-align:left;">Environment variable</th><th style="text-align:left;">Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><code>LEGATE_SHOW_CONFIG=1</code></td><td style="text-align:left;">Print the resolved configuration at startup.</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><code>LEGATE_AUTO_CONFIG=1</code></td><td style="text-align:left;">Detect defaults for unspecified resources (the default). Explicit <code>LEGATE_CONFIG</code> options override those defaults.</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><code>LEGATE_AUTO_CONFIG=0</code></td><td style="text-align:left;">Disable detection and use minimal defaults: one CPU task processor, no GPUs, and a small system-memory allocation. Specify the resources your program needs.</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><code>LEGATE_CONFIG</code></td><td style="text-align:left;">Space-separated runtime options, such as <code>&quot;--gpus 1 --fbmem 4096&quot;</code>.</td></tr></tbody></table><p>To select one GPU while keeping automatic memory sizing:</p><div class="language-bash vp-adaptive-theme"><button title="Copy Code" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">bash</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark vp-code" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">export</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;"> LEGATE_AUTO_CONFIG</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">=</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">1</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">export</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;"> LEGATE_CONFIG</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">=</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;">&quot;--gpus 1 --cpus 1&quot;</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0;">julia</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;"> --project</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> myscript.jl</span></span></code></pre></div><p>Automatic memory sizing can still reserve most of the available memory. For a shared machine, set memory limits as well. For example, this fully manual configuration requests one GPU, one CPU task processor, 4 GiB of system memory, and 4 GiB of device memory <strong>per GPU</strong> (<code>--fbmem</code>):</p><div class="language-bash vp-adaptive-theme"><button title="Copy Code" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">bash</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark vp-code" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">export</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;"> LEGATE_AUTO_CONFIG</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">=</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">0</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">export</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;"> LEGATE_CONFIG</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">=</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;">&quot;--gpus 1 --cpus 1 --sysmem 4096 --fbmem 4096&quot;</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0;">julia</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;"> --project</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> myscript.jl</span></span></code></pre></div><p>Choose memory sizes that fit your workload and leave room for Julia, CUDA, runtime overhead, and other processes. These settings reserve runtime memory pools. They do not cap the entire process&#39;s memory usage.</p><h2 id="Inspect-the-configuration" tabindex="-1">Inspect the configuration <a class="header-anchor" href="#Inspect-the-configuration" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Inspect the configuration {#Inspect-the-configuration}&quot;">​</a></h2><p>After starting Julia with your chosen configuration, print a summary:</p><div class="language-julia vp-adaptive-theme"><button title="Copy Code" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">julia</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark vp-code" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">using</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;"> cuNumeric</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">cuNumeric</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">.</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">versioninfo</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">()</span></span></code></pre></div><p>This includes hardware support, the auto-config setting, the active GPU count, and build details. When <code>LEGATE_AUTO_CONFIG=0</code>, it also prints the <code>LEGATE_CONFIG</code> string. With auto-configuration enabled, that field reads <code>auto</code>.</p><p>To see the full resolved settings, including automatically selected memory sizes, enable configuration output when starting Julia:</p><div class="language-bash vp-adaptive-theme"><button title="Copy Code" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">bash</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark vp-code" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">LEGATE_SHOW_CONFIG</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">=</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;">1</span><span style="--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0;"> julia</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;"> --project</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;"> -e</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> &#39;using cuNumeric&#39;</span></span></code></pre></div><p>To list the options supported by the installed runtime:</p><div class="language-bash vp-adaptive-theme"><button title="Copy Code" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">bash</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark vp-code" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">LEGATE_CONFIG</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">=</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;">&quot;--help&quot;</span><span style="--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0;"> julia</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;"> --project</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;"> -e</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> &#39;using cuNumeric&#39;</span></span></code></pre></div><p>The help command prints the runtime options and exits. No separate Python environment or <code>legate</code> launcher is needed for these Julia commands.</p><h2 id="Processor-and-memory-options" tabindex="-1">Processor and memory options <a class="header-anchor" href="#Processor-and-memory-options" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Processor and memory options {#Processor-and-memory-options}&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Processor counts apply to each Legate process (rank). Memory values below are in <strong>MiB</strong> (1024 MiB = 1 GiB).</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th style="text-align:left;">Option</th><th style="text-align:left;">Resource controlled</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><code>--gpus N</code></td><td style="text-align:left;">Number of visible GPUs to use. <code>0</code> disables GPU task execution.</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><code>--cpus N</code></td><td style="text-align:left;">Number of CPU task processors. This does not set Julia&#39;s thread count.</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><code>--sysmem M</code></td><td style="text-align:left;">System-memory pool per process.</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><code>--fbmem M</code></td><td style="text-align:left;">Device-memory pool <strong>per GPU</strong>. Two GPUs with <code>--fbmem 4096</code> reserve 8 GiB in total.</td></tr></tbody></table><p>For CPU task execution with four task processors and an 8 GiB memory pool:</p><div class="language-bash vp-adaptive-theme"><button title="Copy Code" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">bash</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark vp-code" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">LEGATE_AUTO_CONFIG</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">=</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;">0</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;"> LEGATE_CONFIG</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">=</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;">&quot;--gpus 0 --cpus 4 --sysmem 8192&quot;</span><span style="--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0;"> julia</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;"> --project</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> myscript.jl</span></span></code></pre></div><h2 id="Select-GPUs-and-share-a-machine" tabindex="-1">Select GPUs and share a machine <a class="header-anchor" href="#Select-GPUs-and-share-a-machine" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Select GPUs and share a machine {#Select-GPUs-and-share-a-machine}&quot;">​</a></h2><p><code>--gpus</code> is a count, not a list of device IDs. Use <code>CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES</code> to select devices before starting Julia. For example, on a machine with GPUs 0–3:</p><div class="language-bash vp-adaptive-theme"><button title="Copy Code" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">bash</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark vp-code" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">=</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;">0,2</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;"> LEGATE_AUTO_CONFIG</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">=</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;">0</span><span style="--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0;"> \\</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;">  LEGATE_CONFIG=&quot;--gpus 2 --cpus 1 --sysmem 4096 --fbmem 4096&quot;</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;"> \\</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;">  julia</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;"> --project</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> myscript.jl</span></span></code></pre></div><p>The same <code>--fbmem</code> value applies to each selected GPU. If their capacities differ, choose a value that fits the smallest selected device, or exclude it. On a scheduler-managed cluster, respect the GPU visibility and CPU allocation assigned to your job.</p><p>For concurrent jobs, give each process its own devices where possible and budget host memory across all processes. If startup fails while reserving GPU memory, check device usage with <code>nvidia-smi</code>, choose an available GPU, or lower <code>--fbmem</code>. If host-memory reservation fails, try lowering <code>--sysmem</code>.</p><h2 id="Further-reference" tabindex="-1">Further reference <a class="header-anchor" href="#Further-reference" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Further reference {#Further-reference}&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The options above are documented in the archived Legate 26.06.01 <a href="https://github.com/nv-legate/legate/blob/v26.06.01/docs/legate/source/manual/usage/running.rst" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">runtime guide</a> and <a href="https://github.com/nv-legate/legate/blob/v26.06.01/src/cpp/legate/runtime/detail/argument_parsing/parse.cc" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">runtime option definitions</a>. These versioned source references replace links to the retired documentation site. Use <code>LEGATE_CONFIG=&quot;--help&quot;</code> for the options available in your installed version.</p><p>The same <code>LEGATE_CONFIG</code> string can carry logging / profiling flags (for example <code>--logging legate=debug --log-to-file</code>). Those are covered under <a href="/cuNumeric.jl/stable/debugging#Trace-Legate-runtime-work">Debugging</a>, including how they pair with <a href="/cuNumeric.jl/stable/api_preferences#Task-scope-names">CNPreferences</a> task-scope naming.</p>`,32)])])}const g=s(n,[["render",o]]);export{u as __pageData,g as default};
